2. PLATEAU PHASE (epochs 18-25):
   Val top-1 oscillated in a 0.75pp band (90.75% - 91.50%).
   Val loss oscillated in a 0.009 band (1.1755 - 1.1846).
   No sustained improvement after epoch 18 -- model was essentially saturated.
   The best accuracy (91.50%) was reached at epochs 23-24, but only 0.25pp above epoch 18.

3. TRAIN ACCURACY TRAJECTORY:
   Reached 98.65% immediately at epoch 16 (warmup!) and climbed to 99.88% by epoch 24.
   The model memorized the training set almost completely.
   Without MixUp/CutMix, there is no regularization from soft labels, so the model
   easily overfits training data -- the question is whether this hurts generalization.

--- TRAIN-VAL GAP ANALYSIS ---

Train-val loss gap across all epochs:
  ep16: 0.287 (warmup, large because val loss inflated)
  ep17: 0.251, ep18: 0.265, ep19: 0.272, ep20: 0.282
  ep21: 0.276, ep22: 0.282, ep23: 0.283, ep24: 0.288, ep25: 0.291

The gap WIDENED from 0.251 (ep17) to 0.291 (ep25) = +0.040 over 9 epochs.
This is a moderate widening. The gap stabilized around 0.28-0.29 during late decay,
indicating the cosine LR schedule prevented runaway overfitting.

Train-val accuracy gap:
